    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive engine is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (76.64) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92), representing the most reliable assets on the board. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong lineup position in the two-hole against a mediocre Phillips; his dual-threat capability remains our primary engine for maintaining SB volume. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws the highest situational boost of the day (+14%) due to a favorable dynamic platoon split against Rocker, ensuring he is our premier UTIL play. **Seiya Suzuki** (72.26) also provides elite output, capitalizing on a favorable park factor and a high SP skill adjustment against Feltner, making him a must-start despite the neutral platoon dynamic.\n\nThe decision to slot **Josh Naylor** (69.19) into the 1B spot over secondary depth was driven largely by the park factor at play, which offers a significant +16% lift that overcomes Bradish's respectable metrics. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing** (51.61) and **Cole Young** (50.51). While **Cole Young** sits near the floor, his status as the leadoff hitter keeps him relevant for runs scored, though his low raw projection suggests he is a candidate to be replaced should we need to pivot for more stability. **Alex Freeland** remains our most vulnerable starter at 46.52; while his switch-hitting provides some flexibility, his spot at the bottom of the order severely suppresses his run-production ceiling.\n\nRegarding the bench, the absence of **Jose Caballero** and **James Wood** due to scheduling leaves us without our high-end speed substitutes today. With **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** still sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is tested. We are currently leaning on the internal consistency of the active lineup, but if **Dalton Rushing**'s production continues to drift toward his floor, we may need to look toward the recovery timelines of **Austin Riley** or **Giancarlo Stanton** to provide more impact upon their return. Monitor weather reports for the Bradish start, as any wind shifts could further compress the value of **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young** in an already high-variance matchup.",
